{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546503-the-orders-and-their-necromancers","id":1546503,"title":"The Orders and their Necromancers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-30T12:01:58-08:00","id":1546503,"title":"The Orders and their Necromancers","content":"I was wondering if someone could offer me an example of a Necromancer (Moros specializing in the Death Arcanum) each of the five Orders?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","user":"Darklander","date":".  clarification 12-04-2024, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24961-darklander","name":"Darklander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T16:25:26-08:00","id":1546504,"title":"","content":"This is a repost of something I wrote up years ago:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Teatime</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardian of the Veil manages a network of Ghosts who steal memories of supernatural events. However, he gets increasingly more distracted by analyzing the effect of different memories on his charges. Some of the Ghosts are undergoing shifts in personality as they get more overburdened.<br /> <br /> Thearch studies how Ceremonies of hedge practitioners are able to interact with Ghosts, corpses and other deathly phenomena. She alters the variables of Ceremonies with her Supernal magic to see how she can influence their outcomes. So far, her Shielding magic prevented any major harm.<br /> <br /> Thearch is organizing a group to raid the Underworld for Dissonance-free resources for their Order's Cryptopolies. They don't care about the disruption they cause to that environment. They're currently studying how to turn Ghosts into life-extending medicine, even though Ladder management worries that such could interfere with Awakenings.<br /> <br /> Mystagogue studies all sorts of undead to see how their natures interact with Pancryptia. He suspects that their attunement to Death may erase signs of their passing, like the &quot;Without a Trace&quot; spell. He's currently fascinated by how difficult Vampires are to catch on camera.<br /> <br /> Mystagogue runs a black market of cadavers. She sells body parts for transplants and sacraments, perfected leather and bones for magic, and miscellaneous leftovers as monster food. The Ministry of Mammon are increasingly frustrated by having her as competition.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow started by weaponizing zombies. Now he uses creative taxidermy and embalming to create undead chimeras, big and small. He wants to recreate a hungry monstrosity he and his Order once destroyed.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow styles herself as a mythical psychopomp, escorting Ghosts from Upper Reaches to a Dominion of their preference. She has to fight spiteful Ghosts, Chtonians and all kinds of bizarre Underworld phenomena.<br /> <br /> Free Councilor collects bodies of people in coma and enables his Ghost friends to Claim them. The undead are vouched for and trustworthy, but the sloppy coverup got Sleeper investigators on his trail. It's only a matter of time until Hunters notice.<br /> <br /> Free Councilor wants to create a comprehensive archive of Soul Marks caused by different kinds of near death experiences, in order to aid psychological treatment. She doesn't know the Consillium is suspecting her of being a Reaper.<br /> <br /> Free Councilor routinely summons a Supernal Entity to resurrect people without risk of further Dissonance. He addresses the problem of Soullessness by summoning the subject's Astral Walker and letting them inhabit the body. She currently seeks a replacement that doesn't make her patients so obsessive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guardian of the Veil specializes in the most off-putting aspects of necromancy - human sacrifice, soul theft, shadowy demons... She decided none should be trusted with knowledge of that caliber, but if that knowledge is ever necessary for the wellbeing of the Consilium, she will be the expert to dole it out.<br /> <br /> Thearch governs a traditional community by using spirits of local ancestors as his proxies. He's frustrated by Sleepers heeding advice of monsters, and by his role in that, but if the people trust their families more than advice of an expert, then so be it.<br /> <br /> Mystagogue delights in exploring the Underworld, equipped with the best caving equipment and Imbued Items her position allows her. She's half ethnographer, half poverty tourist, will all the sunny detachment from the plight of the dead that entails.<br /> <br /> Adamantine Arrow focuses on honoring ghosts of fallen heroes through his actions, and occasionally summons them to aid in his battles. Many dead soldiers would rather rest at their graves than be thrown into new battles, but the Arrow does not have the good sense to accept that yet.<br /> <br /> Free Councilor is part of a insurgent cell in a war-torn country. She creates zombies as suicide bombers against servants of the Throne, and all ideologically aligned with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":7593,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","user":"Teatime","date":". 12-02-2024, 06:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-01T16:40:24-08:00","id":1546523,"title":"","content":"The Arrow you spoke of Teatime with the chimera zombies reminds me of Frankenstein, a concept I have for a FC Moros who does exactly that, sew corpses together and then raises them against Seers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T03:05:06-08:00","id":1546532,"title":"","content":"When mentioning the &quot;hungry monstrosity&quot;, I was leaning on the Amkhata from <i>Mummy: the Curse</i>. The idea was that the Arrow became Obssessed over a necromantic sin against nature and is naively trying to recreate it with Supernal power. Regardless of the character's motivation, creative taxidermy is a great method of <i>bedazzling</i> your zombies. A classic one too. Lovecraft did that in a story of his set in Egypt (featuring Harry Houdini).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-02T04:29:04-08:00","id":1546534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darklander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1546503-the-orders-and-their-necromancers#post1546503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering if someone could offer me an example of a Necromancer from each of the five Orders?</div> </div> </div> </div>Necromancer as in a Moros focusing on the Death Arcanum, necromancer as in the popcultural sense of raising the dead as their minions, or necromancer as in the classical sense of communicating with the dead as divination?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}